The built-in BPL responder follows the proxy added to that repository in 2026
by Keith Conger, under the same terms, and the WSdev wiki page
https://ws.nesdev.org/wiki/WonderGate/bplXX.mopera.ne.jp (CC0 1.0).
WonderGate protocol facts cite https://ws.nesdev.org/wiki/WonderGate (CC0 1.0).

Mednafen, Mesen 2, MiSTer, ares, StoicGoose and ARMV30MZ were consulted only
as behaviour references. No code from them is included.

Revival server responses, rankings and selections are newly authored. No
original server code, server data or archived downloads are included.

Files marked "SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT" in crates/ws-wondergate-server
port the private WonderGate revival Python server's protocol.py, shared.py,
store.py, runtime.py, plugins/wave2_history.py, title-handler response semantics,
query/form validation and the complete service tests. The bounded JSON
interpreter and schema infrastructure are newly authored. Title-specific
response policy lives in data files, with provenance marked new.
